$image2image — Qwen-Rapid-AIO image edit (comfy_lib in-process)

SUMMARY
  Edits images[] with a prompt using your local Qwen-Rapid-AIO checkpoint via
  comfy_lib + Qwen-Rapid-AIO_4.json workflow (native Comfy FP8 load, no server).
  Default model: sfw-v23 (Qwen-Rapid-AIO-SFW-v23.safetensors)

SYNTAX
  $image2image
  $image2image(use_all=True)
  $image2image(gpu=True)
  $image2image(model='nsfw-v23')
  $image2image(width=720, height=1280, steps=4, seed=42)

INPUT
  images[]  — source image(s)
  prompts[] — edit instruction (or instruction body / prompt= arg)

OUTPUT
  images[] — one output per job (see use_all)

ARGUMENTS
  use_all=  — when true, send up to 3 reference images into one edit job (Comfy encode limit)
  model=    — model name (sfw-v23, nsfw-v23), checkpoint filename, or path under models/qwen-rapid/
  gpu=      — use CUDA when true (default true; or AH_IMAGE2IMAGE_GPU=0 for CPU)
  prompt=   — same prompt for every job (overrides prompts[])
  width=    — output width (default: input image width, snapped to 8px)
  height=   — output height (default: input image height, snapped to 8px)
  steps=    — inference steps (default 4)
  seed=     — fixed seed; omit for random per job

MODELS
  sfw-v23  — Qwen-Rapid-AIO-SFW-v23.safetensors (default)
  nsfw-v23 — Qwen-Rapid-AIO-NSFW-v23.safetensors
  Workflow: comfy_workflows/Qwen-Rapid-AIO_4.json

DEPENDENCIES
  ComfyUI-compatible Python with comfy_aimdo (e.g. G:\ComfyUI_V\.venv).
  Set AH_COMFY_PYTHON to that python.exe if auto-detect fails.

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_COMFY_PYTHON — ComfyUI venv python (recommended)
  AH_IMAGE2IMAGE_GPU=0 — force CPU
  AH_IMAGE2IMAGE_WORKER=1 — warm subprocess (default)
  AH_EMULATE_IMAGE2IMAGE=1 — placeholder PNGs, no model load

SAMPLING
  Matches Comfy Qwen-Rapid-AIO_4.json: TextEncodeQwenImageEditPlus, KSampler
  sa_solver + beta scheduler, cfg=1, EmptyLatentImage 720×1280.

EXAMPLES
  @fixed: $image2image
  correct the hands

  @blend: @photos -> $image2image(use_all=True)
  combine these references into one portrait

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  Yes — prompts[] cleared; images[] replaced with outputs.
